# UNLOCK — Database & Persistence

Canonical truth: committed migrations + relevant ADRs + `docs/DATABASE.md` / `PERSISTENCE_SCHEMA_V1.md`.

Guardrails:
- evolve forward from current schema; do not rewrite accepted historical migrations;
- preserve constraints, historical evidence/version references, and archive semantics;
- multi-write atomic use cases use one transaction-bound connection;
- rollback/release correctly and do not mask original errors;
- reason explicitly about concurrency when integrity can race;
- Answer Option persistence is already decided/implemented — do not treat it as TBD;
- current authorization baseline is explicit server-side authorization; do not add RLS automatically;
- Claude/agents do not link/push hosted Supabase or apply hosted migrations autonomously.

Use the smallest relevant schema/PGlite/real-Postgres evidence and state environment limits honestly.
